---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SourcesNote from "../components/SourcesNote.astro";
import { figures } from "../data/site";

const rows = [
  ["Starting point, raw land", `${figures.priorAnnualTax} a year`, "Building Bastrop County"],
  ["EdgeConneX during the abatement", `${figures.edgeAbatementPublic} to the county and ISD`, "Building Bastrop County"],
  ["EdgeConneX, ISD projection", `${figures.isdAnnualProjection} a year · ${figures.isdDecadeProjection} over 10 years`, "Tomorrow Begins Here"],
  ["Pacifico at the full rate", `${figures.pacificoAnnualTax} a year`, "Building Bastrop County"],
  ["Pacifico’s published share", `${figures.pacificoCountyShare} of county revenue`, "Building Bastrop County"],
];
---

<Layout
  title="Tax base"
  description="How data centers change Bastrop County’s tax roll: from about $25,000 a year on raw land to commercial payments that fund schools without adding students."
>
  <PageHero
    kicker="The tax base"
    title="A commercial payer that does not bring a town with it."
    lede="Bastrop County has long asked houses to carry schools, the courthouse, and emergency services. A data center is the opposite shape of development: a very large taxable asset and a very small service demand."
  />

  <article class="copy mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 md:px-6 md:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.85fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="max-w-xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Before these projects, the acres in question produced about {figures.priorAnnualTax} a year. That is ranchland
          math. It does not build a high school, staff a fire station, or take weight off a homestead.
        </p>
        <p>
          EdgeConneX won Cedar Creek over {figures.competingSites} other sites. A ten-year abatement was part of
          landing it. Building Bastrop County reports that even during that discount, the county and Bastrop ISD still
          receive more than {figures.edgeAbatementPublic}. The discount is the reason the campus is here. It is not a
          permanent exemption. When it ends, the full commercial value — phase one at {figures.edgePhase}, full
          buildout above {figures.edgeFull} — is what the roll taxes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tomorrow Begins Here publishes a separate ISD figure for that proposal: {figures.isdAnnualProjection} a year, {figures.isdDecadeProjection} over ten years, without the students who would otherwise spend it. Those two
          publications are not the same line item. This page shows both. It does not add them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-line bg-paper">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">Published tax figures for Bastrop County data center land</caption>
          <thead class="bg-pine text-paper">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium" scope="col">Line</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium" scope="col">Published figure</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              rows.map((row) => (
                <tr class="border-t border-line align-top">
                  <th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium" scope="row">
                    {row[0]}
                    <span class="mt-1 block text-xs font-normal text-muted">{row[2]}</span>
                  </th>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed md:text-sm">{row[1]}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="rounded-3xl bg-sand p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl">Schools</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The new taxable value arrives without a new enrollment class. Building Bastrop County’s framing is direct:
          the revenue can go to teacher pay, buildings, and technology, because it is not consumed by {figures.subdivisionStudents} additional students the way a 1,000-home subdivision would require.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl bg-sand p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl">County services</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Fire engines, EMS, and the county budget are funded by the levy. A campus that brings its own security and
          suppression adds a payer and not a new neighborhood of calls. Pacifico’s full-rate payment is published at
          more than {figures.pacificoCountyShare} of county revenue from that project alone.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl bg-sand p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl">Homeowners</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
          When more of the levy comes from a commercial asset, the same public services do not have to be carried only
          by houses. That is the relief. It is a change in who pays, not a coupon printed on one tax statement.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl">Pacifico stepped off the abatement</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Pacifico Energy and BlackChamber Partners withdrew their Chapter 312 and JETI applications. Building Bastrop
        County reports the Cedar Creek campus will pay full property taxes: {figures.pacificoAnnualTax} a year on a {figures.pacificoInvestment} project with {figures.pacificoPower} of on-site generation. That is the cleanest
        version of the argument. No discount period. A full commercial bill, and still almost no students, almost no
        daily traffic, and a potable draw published at {figures.pacificoDailyWater} a day.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        EdgeConneX is the competitive version of the same idea. The abatement is what kept a {figures.edgeFull} campus from landing at one of the other {figures.competingSites} sites. During the discount, the public
        entities still collect orders of magnitude more than the {figures.priorAnnualTax} the land paid before.
        After the discount, the county keeps the building.
      </p>
    </section>

    <SourcesNote />
  </article>
</Layout>
